WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.605
Tom and Becky had lost track of time.

2
00:00:03.606 --> 00:00:07.246
Their candles had gone out, and they both had fallen asleep.

3
00:00:07.247 --> 00:00:12.055
Had they slept long? Tom wondered. There was no way of knowing.

4
00:00:12.056 --> 00:00:15.477
"I'm so hungry," said Becky.

5
00:00:15.478 --> 00:00:22.468
"Here." Tom passed her some cake. "I saved this for you."

6
00:00:22.469 --> 00:00:26.099
"Are people looking for us?" asked Becky.

7
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.524
"Sure," said Tom.

8
00:00:28.525 --> 00:00:34.598
But he knew the cave was big, and if he and Becky waited to be found, they might wait forever.

9
00:00:34.599 --> 00:00:37.884
"I think I should explore," he said.

10
00:00:37.885 --> 00:00:41.798
"Here, hold one end of this kite string.

11
00:00:41.799 --> 00:00:47.928
I will go down these side passages as far as I can, and then I'll come back."

12
00:00:47.929 --> 00:00:51.611
Becky was scared, but she agreed to Tom's plan.

13
00:00:51.612 --> 00:00:56.150
Tom crawled slowly into the dark, feeling in front of him like a blind man.

14
00:00:56.151 --> 00:00:59.532
He had only gone a short distance when he heard something.

15
00:00:59.533 --> 00:01:04.835
He gave a shout, and his voice echoed eerily throughout the cave.

16
00:01:04.836 --> 00:01:06.714
Then a light appeared.

17
00:01:06.715 --> 00:01:11.122
When Tom saw who was holding the light, he almost shouted again.

18
00:01:11.123 --> 00:01:13.925
The face in the light was Injun Joe's!

19
00:01:13.926 --> 00:01:21.274
Injun Joe looked just as scared to see Tom. He bolted away from him.

20
00:01:21.275 --> 00:01:25.737
When Tom crawled back to Becky, she asked him why he had shouted.

21
00:01:25.738 --> 00:01:28.424
"Just for luck," said Tom.

22
00:01:28.425 --> 00:01:32.284
He didn't want to make Becky more afraid than she already was.

23
00:01:32.285 --> 00:01:37.650
Then he said, "I think I can find a way out, but I need some more luck."

24
00:01:37.651 --> 00:01:39.990
He leaned forward and kissed Becky.

25
00:01:39.991 --> 00:01:45.033
Then he crawled down a different passage.

26
00:01:45.034 --> 00:01:49.495
Kissing Becky had indeed brought Tom some luck.

27
00:01:49.496 --> 00:01:58.078
Soon Tom saw light again, but this was a different kind of light—sunlight shining through a small hole.

28
00:01:58.079 --> 00:02:04.268
Tom took out his knife and gradually made the hole big enough to squeeze through.

29
00:02:04.269 --> 00:02:09.278
After Tom and Becky climbed out of the cave, Tom covered the hole with some leaves.

30
00:02:09.279 --> 00:02:13.280
He didn't want Injun Joe to find it and escape the same way.

31
00:02:13.281 --> 00:02:20.539
When Tom realized where they were, he exclaimed, "Gosh, we're five miles downriver from town!

32
00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:24.595
We walked almost two miles underground."

33
00:02:24.596 --> 00:02:30.284
Tom and Becky walked to the river and got a barge that was headed upriver to stop for them.

34
00:02:30.285 --> 00:02:35.241
The crew on the barge had heard about the missing children, so they agreed to take them home.

35
00:02:35.242 --> 00:02:38.846
The town rejoiced, and then the two children were put to bed.

36
00:02:38.847 --> 00:02:44.139
Becky stayed in bed for almost four days, but Tom felt better after

37
00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:50.402
two. Tom learned that Huck had been sick as well, so Tom went to visit his friend at the Welshman's

38
00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:56.133
house. When Tom and Huck were alone, Tom told Huck that he thought he knew where the treasure

39
00:02:56.134 --> 00:02:59.993
was. Huck shook his head and said, "It isn't in the tavern,

40
00:02:59.994 --> 00:03:04.310
Tom." Tom wanted to interrupt his friend, but Huck was talking too

41
00:03:04.311 --> 00:03:10.151
fast. "When I was sick," said Huck, "I dreamed a lot, and I guess I did a lot of

42
00:03:10.152 --> 00:03:15.986
talking. I talked about the tavern, I talked about Injun Joe and the murder, and I talked about the Widow

43
00:03:15.987 --> 00:03:19.272
Douglas. The Welshman and others figured things out and searched the

44
00:03:19.273 --> 00:03:21.741
tavern. But all they found was

45
00:03:21.742 --> 00:03:24.700
whiskey." Tom smiled. "Of

46
00:03:24.701 --> 00:03:27.959
course! That's all they found because the gold is in the

47
00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:31.480
cave. I saw Injun Joe in the

48
00:03:31.481 --> 00:03:36.842
cave." "The night you were found, Judge Thatcher blocked the cave entrance with an iron door," said

49
00:03:36.843 --> 00:03:40.376
Huck. "He didn't want what happened to you and Becky to happen

50
00:03:40.377 --> 00:03:43.049
again." Tom wanted to go to the

51
00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:48.369
judge. But the Widow Douglas, who had been taking care of Huck at the Welshman's house, wouldn't let Huck

52
00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:53.300
go. So Tom went by himself, and then headed back to the cave with the judge and the

53
00:03:53.301 --> 00:03:56.348
sheriff. The judge opened the great iron door with his

54
00:03:56.349 --> 00:04:01.068
key. Inside they found Injun Joe lying dead on the

55
00:04:01.069 --> 00:04:05.871
ground. His knife was broken at his side where he had tried to chip his way

56
00:04:05.872 --> 00:04:11.669
out. The next day Tom got Huck. They borrowed a rowboat, and Tom rowed

57
00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:14.793
downriver. Tom found his secret entrance to the cave

58
00:04:14.794 --> 00:04:18.878
easily. They each lit a candle and

59
00:04:18.879 --> 00:04:24.590
entered. Tom showed Huck where he and Becky had slept, and then he led Huck to where he had seen Injun

60
00:04:24.591 --> 00:04:26.930
Joe. They climbed down into the

61
00:04:26.931 --> 00:04:32.109
chamber. Tom and Huck both noticed the large cross on the wall, and they immediately started

62
00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:36.566
digging. They didn't have to dig long before they came to a

63
00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:40.519
board. They lifted the board, and under it was a small

64
00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:46.885
compartment. Inside the compartment were some candles, some matches, and a box full of silver and

65
00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:51.328
gold. "Finally!" exclaimed Huck. "We found the

66
00:04:51.329 --> 00:04:57.898
treasure!" "Even when money's free," said Tom, "you still have to work for

67
00:04:57.899 --> 00:05:26.053
it."

